  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q10-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Let $n$ be odd. By expanding the right-hand side, show that\n$$a^n+b^n=(a+b)(a^{n-1}-a^{n-2}b+\\cdots-ab^{n-2}+b^{n-1}).$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a^n+b^n$.\n\nThe intermediate terms cancel; since $n$ is odd, the final term is $+b^n$.",
      "worked": "Let $S=a^{n-1}-a^{n-2}b+\\cdots-ab^{n-2}+b^{n-1}$. Expanding gives\n$$\\begin{align*}(a+b)S&=\\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}(-1)^j a^{n-j}b^j+\\sum_{j=1}^{n}(-1)^{j-1}a^{n-j}b^j\\\\(a+b)S&=a^n+\\sum_{j=1}^{n-1}\\bigl((-1)^j+(-1)^{j-1}\\bigr)a^{n-j}b^j+(-1)^{n-1}b^n\\\\(a+b)S&=a^n+b^n.\\end{align*}$$\nEach intermediate coefficient is zero, and $n-1$ is even.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
